Prepare a bounded, source-versioned evidence slice for generateConcepts. Invent distinct reuse concepts that exploit the building’s known characteristics while respecting supplied constraints. Describe functional organization and phasing, preserve uncertainty about unverified conditions, and avoid presenting conceptual layouts as certified engineering designs. Include direct observations, current authority, contrary evidence, a plausible rival interpretation, and missing decisive fields. Carry forward the actual prior-stage records when provided.
